<main>
<section class="hero">
 <div class="container">
  <div class="badge">🗺️ Career Exploration Guide</div>
  <h1>Explore <span class="gradient">Career Paths in Tech</span></h1>
  <p class="lead">Discover roles, required skills, salary ranges, and real companies hiring.</p>
 </div>
</section>

<section>
 <div class="container">
  <h2>Popular Tech Career Paths</h2>
  <p style="color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:30px">Here are some of the most in-demand roles for students and early graduates:</p>
  
  <div class="grid">
   <div class="card">
    <div class="icon">⚙️</div>
    <h3>Backend Engineer</h3>
    <p>Build server-side systems, APIs, databases, and infrastructure.</p>
    <div class="salary">$85K – $150K</div>
    <h4 style="margin-top:15px;font-size:1rem;color:var(--accent)">Key Skills:</h4>
    <div>
     <span class="skill-tag">Node.js / Python</span>
     <span class="skill-tag">Databases</span>
     <span class="skill-tag">APIs</span>
     <span class="skill-tag">SQL</span>
    </div>
   </div>

   <div class="card">
    <div class="icon">🎨</div>
    <h3>Frontend Engineer</h3>
    <p>Build user interfaces, web applications, and responsive designs.</p>
    <div class="salary">$80K – $140K</div>
    <h4 style="margin-top:15px;font-size:1rem;color:var(--accent)">Key Skills:</h4>
    <div>
     <span class="skill-tag">React / Vue</span>
     <span class="skill-tag">JavaScript</span>
     <span class="skill-tag">CSS</span>
     <span class="skill-tag">HTML</span>
    </div>
   </div>

   <div class="card">
    <div class="icon">🔗</div>
    <h3>Full-Stack Developer</h3>
    <p>Handle both frontend and backend, end-to-end product development.</p>
    <div class="salary">$90K – $160K</div>
    <h4 style="margin-top:15px;font-size:1rem;color:var(--accent)">Key Skills:</h4>
    <div>
     <span class="skill-tag">React</span>
     <span class="skill-tag">Node.js</span>
     <span class="skill-tag">Databases</span>
     <span class="skill-tag">Deployment</span>
    </div>
   </div>

   <div class="card">
    <div class="icon">📊</div>
    <h3>Data Engineer</h3>
    <p>Build data pipelines, warehouses, and analytics infrastructure.</p>
    <div class="salary">$90K – $155K</div>
    <h4 style="margin-top:15px;font-size:1rem;color:var(--accent)">Key Skills:</h4>
    <div>
     <span class="skill-tag">SQL</span>
     <span class="skill-tag">Python</span>
     <span class="skill-tag">ETL</span>
     <span class="skill-tag">Data Warehouses</span>
    </div>
   </div>

   <div class="card">
    <div class="icon">🤖</div>
    <h3>AI/ML Engineer</h3>
    <p>Develop machine learning models and AI systems.</p>
    <div class="salary">$100K – $180K</div>
    <h4 style="margin-top:15px;font-size:1rem;color:var(--accent)">Key Skills:</h4>
    <div>
     <span class="skill-tag">Python</span>
     <span class="skill-tag">TensorFlow</span>
     <span class="skill-tag">Math</span>
     <span class="skill-tag">Data</span>
    </div>
   </div>

   <div class="card">
    <div class="icon">🛡️</div>
    <h3>DevOps Engineer</h3>
    <p>Manage infrastructure, deployment pipelines, and system reliability.</p>
    <div class="salary">$95K – $160K</div>
    <h4 style="margin-top:15px;font-size:1rem;color:var(--accent)">Key Skills:</h4>
    <div>
     <span class="skill-tag">Docker</span>
     <span class="skill-tag">Kubernetes</span>
     <span class="skill-tag">Linux</span>
     <span class="skill-tag">AWS / Cloud</span>
    </div>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
</section>

<section>
 <div class="container">
  <h2>Career Path Examples</h2>
  <p style="color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:30px">Here are realistic paths for students entering tech:</p>

  <div class="pathway">
   <h4>Path 1: Frontend Developer → Senior Frontend → Tech Lead</h4>
   <p><strong>Timeline:</strong> Year 0–2 (Entry) → Year 2–5 (Senior) → Year 5+ (Leadership)</p>
   <p style="color:var(--muted);margin-top:10px"><strong>Skills to build:</strong> React, JavaScript, CSS, UI/UX basics, performance optimization, team mentoring</p>
   <p style="color:var(--muted);margin-top:10px"><strong>Entry companies:</strong> Startups, agencies, Google, Microsoft, Airbnb</p>
  </div>

  <div class="pathway">
   <h4>Path 2: Backend Engineer → Senior Backend → Architecture</h4>
   <p><strong>Timeline:</strong> Year 0–2 (Entry) → Year 2–5 (Senior) → Year 5+ (Architect)</p>
   <p style="color:var(--muted);margin-top:10px"><strong>Skills to build:</strong> Node.js / Python, Databases, System Design, Cloud infrastructure</p>
   <p style="color:var(--muted);margin-top:10px"><strong>Entry companies:</strong> Tech companies, fintech startups, E-commerce platforms</p>
  </div>

  <div class="pathway">
   <h4>Path 3: Data Analytics → Data Engineer → ML Engineer</h4>
   <p><strong>Timeline:</strong> Year 0–1 (Analytics) → Year 1–3 (Data) → Year 3+ (ML)</p>
   <p style="color:var(--muted);margin-top:10px"><strong>Skills to build:</strong> SQL, Python, Statistics, TensorFlow, Cloud platforms</p>
   <p style="color:var(--muted);margin-top:10px"><strong>Entry companies:</strong> Startups, tech companies, finance, healthcare</p>
  </div>

  <div class="pathway">
   <h4>Path 4: Full-Stack Developer → Startup CTO / Tech Manager</h4>
   <p><strong>Timeline:</strong> Year 0–2 (Individual contributor) → Year 2–4 (Lead) → Year 4+ (CTO/Manager)</p>
   <p style="color:var(--muted);margin-top:10px"><strong>Skills to build:</strong> Full-stack (React, Node, DB), System design, team leadership, product thinking</p>
   <p style="color:var(--muted);margin-top:10px"><strong>Entry companies:</strong> Startups, tech companies, agencies</p>
  </div>
 </div>
</section>

<section>
 <div class="container">
  <h2>How to Start: First Job as a Student</h2>
  
  <div class="grid">
   <div class="card">
    <h3>Internship</h3>
    <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Building real experience, seeing how teams work, exploring roles</p>
    <p style="margin-top:15px;color:var(--muted)">Usually 3–6 months during summer or semester</p>
    <p style="margin-top:10px"><strong>How to land one:</strong> Apply in Jan–Feb for summer roles. Show portfolio or GitHub.</p>
   </div>

   <div class="card">
    <h3>Contract / Freelance</h3>
    <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Building portfolio projects, earning money, flexible scheduling</p>
    <p style="margin-top:15px;color:var(--muted)">Project-based, 1–3 months typically</p>
    <p style="margin-top:10px"><strong>How to land one:</strong> Upwork, Fiverr, local startups, ask your network</p>
   </div>

   <div class="card">
    <h3>Open Source</h3>
    <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Learning, building portfolio, community involvement</p>
    <p style="margin-top:15px;color:var(--muted)">Volunteer, unpaid, but shows real code ability</p>
    <p style="margin-top:10px"><strong>How to start:</strong> GitHub, pick a project you like, contribute small fixes first</p>
   </div>

   <div class="card">
    <h3>Personal Projects</h3>
    <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Learning at your own pace, full ownership, portfolio building</p>
    <p style="margin-top:15px;color:var(--muted)">Self-directed, no external pressure</p>
    <p style="margin-top:10px"><strong>How to start:</strong> Pick a real problem, build a solution, deploy it</p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
</section>

<section>
 <div class="container">
  <h2>Top Companies Hiring New Grads</h2>
  
  <p style="color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:20px">These companies actively hire students and early graduates:</p>

  <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;margin:30px 0">
   <div class="company-list">
    <strong>FAANG + Big Tech</strong><br>
    Google, Meta, Apple, Amazon, Microsoft, Netflix
   </div>
   <div class="company-list">
    <strong>Fast-Growing Tech</strong><br>
    Stripe, Airbnb, Figma, Notion, Discord, Canva
   </div>
   <div class="company-list">
    <strong>Startups (Series B–D)</strong><br>
    Check AngelList, Crater, Y Combinator job boards
   </div>
   <div class="company-list">
    <strong>Non-Tech That Hire Engineers</strong><br>
    McKinsey, Goldman Sachs, JPMorgan, Uber, Lyft
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
</section>

<section>
 <div class="container">
  <h2>What Employers Look For in Student Hires</h2>
  
  <div class="grid">
   <div class="card">
    <div class="icon">💼</div>
    <h3>Portfolio / GitHub</h3>
    <p>Real projects you've built. Shows you can actually code and ship things.</p>
   </div>
   <div class="card">
    <div class="icon">🎓</div>
    <h3>Learning Ability</h3>
    <p>Show you can learn quickly and adapt. Specific tools matter less than attitude.</p>
   </div>
   <div class="card">
    <div class="icon">🤝</div>
    <h3>Communication</h3>
    <p>Can you explain your work? Ask good questions? Collaborate with others?</p>
   </div>
   <div class="card">
    <div class="icon">📈</div>
    <h3>Curiosity & Growth</h3>
    <p>Do you ship things? Iterate? Learn from feedback? That matters more than perfection.</p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
</section>

<section>
 <div class="container">
  <h2>Salary Reality Check</h2>
  
  <div style="background:rgba(110,231,255,.08);border:1px solid rgba(110,231,255,.2);border-radius:16px;padding:25px;margin:30px 0">
   <h3 style="margin-top:0">New Grad / Junior Engineer (0–2 years)</h3>
   <p style="color:var(--muted);margin:15px 0">$70K–$120K base salary + bonus + stock (varies by location and company)</p>
   <p style="font-size:0.95rem"><strong>Reality:</strong> Startup might pay $60K; Google might pay $170K. Location matters. NYC and SF pay 20–30% more than other cities.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="background:rgba(110,231,255,.08);border:1px solid rgba(110,231,255,.2);border-radius:16px;padding:25px;margin:30px 0">
   <h3 style="margin-top:0">Senior (5+ years)</h3>
   <p style="color:var(--muted);margin:15px 0">$150K–$250K+ total compensation</p>
   <p style="font-size:0.95rem"><strong>Note:</strong> These are tech salaries. Remember: focus first on learning and impact, not salary. Salary grows naturally as you get better.</p>
  </div>
 </div>
</section>

<section>
 <div class="container">
  <div style="background:rgba(110,231,255,.08);border:1px solid rgba(110,231,255,.2);border-radius:16px;padding:40px;text-align:center">
   <h2>Ready to Pick a Path?</h2>
   <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:1rem;margin:15px 0">Start by building projects in areas that interest you. Your first job will teach you more than anything else.</p>
